    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d360">

                <pb facs="0368" n="358" xml:id="pg358"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/4517: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Algiers</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wiley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Algiers</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-09-29T23:00:00+01:00">September 29,
                            1943—11 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 30—2:17 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1662. For Lehman from Fryer. Dutch Consul Casablanca has made informal inquiry
                    concerning use of Marechal Lyautey refugee center to house 1500 Dutch refugees
                    for a period of 30 days.</p>
                <p>These refugees are now in Spain. They would be despatched to Casablanca and held
                    there pending Dutch-made arrangements for transportation. We view this project
                    favorably if it will not conflict with Washington–London plans for housing
                    stateless refugees. We assume Dutch will make formal inquiry in Washington and
                    wish to assure you that we can assume all responsibility for taking care of
                    these refugees if you are formally approached by the Dutch and if you approve.
                    We assume that Dutch Government would reimburse the United States Government for
                    expenditures made in its behalf. Should this be brought to your attention
                    formally Dutch Government should advise you of measures it will take in Spain to
                    screen refugees for security purposes in order that this information may be
                    transmitted to G–2 section of HQ. We are advised by Dutch Consul that the French
                    have approved this project. [Fryer.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wiley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
